{"id": "EUVD-2026-97603", "enisaUuid": "c7625d3d-0d40-3afb-83e0-482e595e85c6", "description": "Parse Server before 8.6.95 and 9.0.0 before 9.10.2-alpha.3 does not resolve file references lacking a URL before passing objects to Cloud Code triggers and LiveQuery, causing an uncaught exception that terminates the process. Attackers able to write to a class with Cloud Code save, find, or delete triggers or LiveQuery enabled, including unauthenticated users when public write access or sign-up is allowed, can crash the server or break subsequent requests.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T11:53:10", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/parse-community/parse-server/security/advisories/GHSA-gpr6-gr9g-pfw6", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/parse-server-before-8.6.95-and-9.0.0-before-9.10.2-alpha.3-denial-of-service-via-file-pointer-without-url"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109301", "GHSA-rxj9-xm24-7477"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.35, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "524902e3-bf13-30ef-8f53-d908d03bceab", "product": {"name": "parse-server", "vendor": {"name": "parse-community"}}, "product_version": "9.0.0 <9.10.2-alpha.3"}, {"id": "997926a3-f93f-360d-bace-84c506b5ac8c", "product": {"name": "parse-server", "vendor": {"name": "parse-community"}}, "product_version": "0 <8.6.95"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7a7a3379-d1a6-30f5-9641-a52f3cdf3f72", "vendor": {"name": "parse-community"}}], "isExploited": false}